# Binder MUI Theme

Admin panel frontend (`binder_app_frontend`). Brand source: Binder identity guide (PPT). Default theme: **dark**, with **light** mode and user toggle.

## Architecture

- **Vite** bundles assets and fonts — it has no theme API.
- **MUI `createTheme`** owns colors, typography, spacing, and component defaults.
- **Never** put brand colors or fonts in `vite.config.ts` or `.env`.

```
src/theme/
├── tokens.ts              # raw HEX constants
├── palette.ts             # getPalette('light' | 'dark')
├── typography.ts          # font families and variants
├── components.ts          # Mui* overrides
├── index.ts               # getTheme(mode), exports darkTheme / lightTheme
└── ThemeModeProvider.tsx  # context + localStorage toggle
```

Flow: `tokens` → `palette` + `typography` → `createTheme` + `components` → `ThemeModeProvider` → `ThemeProvider` → MUI components via props.

Replace the current placeholder in `src/theme/index.ts` (MUI default blue/purple) when implementing.

## Brand Color Tokens

Use only these HEX values via `tokens.ts`. Never hardcode in components.

| Token | HEX | Role |
|-------|-----|------|
| `orange.main` | `#F36B20` | Primary actions, active nav |
| `orange.light` | `#FFA00A` | Hover, links on dark bg |
| `orange.dark` | `#F85200` | Pressed states |
| `teal.main` | `#27A59E` | Secondary |
| `teal.light` | `#23CFC5` | Accents, badges, charts |
| `green.main` | `#61BE6B` | Success |
| `green.light` | `#54D462` | Success highlights |
| `neutral.black` | `#101010` | Dark page background |
| `neutral.charcoal` | `#21201F` | Dark surfaces (paper) |
| `neutral.darkWarm` | `#1C1A19` | Elevated surfaces, gradient base |
| `neutral.gray` | `#EDEDED` | Light dividers / secondary text (light mode) |
| `neutral.white` | `#FFFFFF` | Light surfaces / dark-mode primary text |

**Do not use:** PPT embedded theme colors (e.g. Google Slides `#4285F4`), CMYK values, or Arial from the deck.

## Dark Theme (default)

Map to MUI `palette` with `mode: 'dark'`:

| MUI key | Value |
|---------|-------|
| `background.default` | `#101010` |
| `background.paper` | `#21201F` |
| `text.primary` | `#FFFFFF` |
| `text.secondary` | `rgba(237, 237, 237, 0.7)` |
| `divider` | `rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12)` |
| `primary` | orange scale, `contrastText: #FFFFFF` |
| `secondary` | `#23CFC5`, `contrastText: #101010` |
| `success` | `#54D462` |

**Surface hierarchy:** page (`#101010`) → paper (`#21201F`) → elevated (`#1C1A19`).

**Brand gradient** — login/hero layouts only, not global body or data screens:

```
radial-gradient(ellipse at 85% 15%, rgba(35, 207, 197, 0.15), transparent 50%),
radial-gradient(ellipse at 70% 0%, rgba(243, 107, 32, 0.12), transparent 45%),
#101010
```

Define gradient as a theme token or layout component override — not inline HEX in pages.

**Logo on dark:** white version only.

## Light Theme (toggle)

Map to MUI `palette` with `mode: 'light'`:

| MUI key | Value |
|---------|-------|
| `background.default` | `#FFFFFF` |
| `background.paper` | `#FFFFFF` |
| `text.primary` | `#21201F` |
| `text.secondary` | `#434343` |
| `divider` | `#EDEDED` |
| `primary` / `secondary` / `success` | same brand tokens as dark |

**Logo on light:** color or black version.

## Theme Mode Behavior

- **Default:** `dark`
- **Toggle:** persist in `localStorage` key `binder-theme-mode`
- **Fallback:** use `prefers-color-scheme` only when no stored preference
- **Provider:** `ThemeModeProvider` wraps `ThemeProvider` with `useMemo(() => getTheme(mode), [mode])`
- Export `darkTheme`, `lightTheme`, and `getTheme` from `src/theme/index.ts`

## Typography

| Role | Font | MUI mapping |
|------|------|-------------|
| UI / body | Montserrat (Gotham substitute) | `fontFamily`, `body1`, `body2`, `button`, `caption` |
| Headings | DM Serif Display | `h1`–`h4` only |
| Fallback | Verdana, sans-serif | end of `fontFamily` stack |

**Font loading** (prefer bundled fonts):

- **Preferred:** `@fontsource/montserrat` + `@fontsource/dm-serif-display` imported in `src/main.tsx`
- **Alternative:** Google Fonts `<link>` in `index.html`

Montserrat weights: 300, 400, 500, 700, 800.

**Minimum body size:** 14px on `body1` — not the PPT 8pt minimum.

## MUI-First Styling Policy

Avoid CSS directly on components. Customize via the theme so components need minimal styling.

**Preferred order:**

1. MUI props — `color="primary"`, `variant="contained"`, `Typography variant="h2"`
2. Theme `components` overrides in `src/theme/components.ts`
3. `sx` with palette keys — `bgcolor: 'background.paper'`, `color: 'text.secondary'`, `p: 2`
4. `sx` callback — `sx={(theme) => ({ borderColor: theme.palette.divider })}`

**Forbidden unless explicitly approved:**

- `.css` / `.module.css` for component styling
- Inline `style={{ ... }}`
- Hardcoded HEX/RGB in `sx` or components
- `@emotion/styled` / `styled()` for one-off styles
- Global CSS beyond `CssBaseline` and font imports

**Required dark overrides in `components.ts`:**

- `MuiPaper`: `backgroundImage: 'none'`
- `MuiAppBar` / `MuiDrawer`: flat surfaces, `boxShadow: 'none'`, border via `palette.divider`

```tsx
// GOOD
<Button color="primary" variant="contained">Salvar</Button>
<Typography variant="h2">Empresas</Typography>
<Box sx={{ bgcolor: 'background.paper', p: 3 }}>

// BAD
<Box sx={{ bgcolor: '#21201F', color: '#fff' }}>
<div style={{ fontFamily: 'Montserrat' }}>
```

## Do Not Port from PPT

- Slide layouts, mockup frames, funnel graphics, social-post templates
- Full-page gradients on admin/data screens
- Decorative "B" graphic on every screen (login/empty states only)
- Black logo on dark backgrounds
- Verdana as primary font

## Layout Principles (from brand guide)

- Left-aligned text in forms and data views
- Clear hierarchy: title > subtitle > highlights > body
- Generous spacing (`theme.spacing`, default grid 8px)
- Safe margins; aligned icons and elements

## Implementation Checklist

When implementing or updating the theme:

1. Create `tokens.ts` → `palette.ts` → `typography.ts` → `components.ts` → refactor `index.ts`
2. Add font loading (`@fontsource` in `main.tsx` or Google Fonts in `index.html`)
3. Add `ThemeModeProvider` with dark default, toggle, and `localStorage`
4. Wire `App.tsx`: `ThemeModeProvider` → `CssBaseline`
5. Audit components: no hardcoded colors; use palette keys only
6. Add brand logos under `src/assets/brand/` when available
